select c.id, $L$m1-14$L$, $L$Fundamentals of Testing$L$, 1, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$What is testware?$L$, $J$[{"text":"The work products produced during the test activities, such as test plans, test cases, test data, and test reports","correct":true,"why":"Testware is the collective term for artifacts created and used during testing across the whole process."},{"text":"Only the automated test scripts used to run tests","correct":false,"why":"Scripts are one part of testware, but the term covers plans, cases, data, environments, and reports too."},{"text":"The production software under test","correct":false,"why":"The software under test is the test object, not testware."},{"text":"The hardware on which the software runs in production","correct":false,"why":"Production hardware is part of the operational environment, not testware."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$The syllabus defines testware as the work products created during the test process, including test plans, test conditions, test cases, test data, test scripts, test environments, and test reports. Managing testware and its versions is part of good test practice.$L$, $L$The test repository for a banking portal holds the test plan, 300 test cases, seeded customer data, and nightly execution reports, all of which are testware.$L$
