select c.id, $L$m1-16$L$, $L$Fundamentals of Testing$L$, 1, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$Which two generic roles in testing does the syllabus describe?$L$, $J$[{"text":"A test management role and a testing role","correct":true,"why":"The syllabus describes a test management role (organizing and directing) and a testing role (performing the technical testing work)."},{"text":"A debugging role and a coding role","correct":false,"why":"These are development activities and are not the generic testing roles described."},{"text":"A marketing role and a sales role","correct":false,"why":"These are unrelated to the testing roles defined in the syllabus."},{"text":"A requirements role and a deployment role","correct":false,"why":"While related to the lifecycle, these are not the two generic testing roles the syllabus names."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$The syllabus identifies two principal roles: the test management role, responsible for the overall test process and leadership of the test team, and the testing role, responsible for the engineering aspects such as analysis, design, implementation, and execution. One person may perform both depending on context.$L$, $L$On a small startup team building a booking app, one senior engineer plans and reports on testing (management role) while also writing and running the test cases (testing role).$L$
