select c.id, $L$m1-20$L$, $L$Fundamentals of Testing$L$, 1, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$Which activity closes out testing by evaluating whether objectives were met and archiving useful testware?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Test completion","correct":true,"why":"Test completion checks that work is finished, archives reusable testware, reports results, and captures lessons learned."},{"text":"Test analysis","correct":false,"why":"Analysis happens early to identify what to test, not to close out testing."},{"text":"Test monitoring and control","correct":false,"why":"Monitoring and control run throughout to steer progress, but completion is the specific closing activity."},{"text":"Test implementation","correct":false,"why":"Implementation prepares testware to run, which precedes execution and completion."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Test completion occurs at milestones such as a release or iteration end. It ensures activities are finished or documented, archives testware for reuse, produces a test summary report, and feeds lessons learned into future improvement.$L$, $L$After a mobile release, the team archives the automated suite, writes a test summary report, and records that flaky network tests should be stabilized next iteration.$L$
