select c.id, $L$m2-05$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is a good testing practice that applies regardless of the SDLC model in use?$L$, $J$[{"text":"For every development activity there is a corresponding testing activity","correct":true,"why":"This principle holds in any SDLC: testing should shadow development throughout, not appear only at the end."},{"text":"Testing should always be performed only by developers","correct":false,"why":"Who tests varies by context; this is not a universal good practice."},{"text":"Test design should start only after all code is complete","correct":false,"why":"Early test design is encouraged in every model; waiting for all code delays feedback."},{"text":"Each SDLC needs a completely different set of testing principles","correct":false,"why":"Core good practices are common across SDLCs; they are not reinvented per model."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$A recognized good testing practice for any SDLC is that each development activity has a corresponding test activity, so verification and validation accompany development throughout. These practices are model-independent and support early feedback in any lifecycle.$L$, $L$Whether a team runs Scrum or Waterfall, its test lead ensures every requirement written has an associated test condition drafted at the same time.$L$
