select c.id, $L$m2-08$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which approach centers on collaboratively defining acceptance tests, often expressed as concrete examples, before the corresponding functionality is implemented?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Acceptance Test-Driven Development (ATDD)","correct":true,"why":"ATDD derives acceptance tests collaboratively from requirements and examples before implementation."},{"text":"Exploratory testing","correct":false,"why":"Exploratory testing is unscripted learning during execution, not upfront acceptance-test derivation."},{"text":"Load testing","correct":false,"why":"Load testing is a non-functional activity, unrelated to deriving acceptance tests from examples."},{"text":"Boundary value analysis","correct":false,"why":"That is a black-box test technique for choosing values, not a development-driving approach."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$ATDD is a test-first approach in which acceptance tests are created collaboratively from requirements before functionality is built, guiding development toward agreed outcomes. It is one of the ways testing acts as a driver for development.$L$, $L$Before coding a refund feature, a business analyst, developer, and tester agree on example refund scenarios and turn them into acceptance tests that define done.$L$
