select c.id, $L$m2-09$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Behaviour-Driven Development (BDD) primarily aims to do which of the following?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Express desired system behaviour in a readable, shared notation so business and technical stakeholders agree","correct":true,"why":"BDD uses accessible given-when-then style scenarios so all stakeholders share one understanding of behaviour."},{"text":"Replace all unit tests with performance tests","correct":false,"why":"BDD is about shared behavioural understanding, not swapping test types."},{"text":"Remove business stakeholders from the testing conversation","correct":false,"why":"BDD deliberately includes business stakeholders through readable scenarios."},{"text":"Guarantee full code coverage automatically","correct":false,"why":"BDD improves shared understanding; it does not by itself guarantee coverage."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$BDD expresses intended behaviour in a natural, structured language that both business and technical people understand, improving communication and turning examples into executable tests. Like TDD and ATDD, it is a test-first approach that drives development.$L$, $L$A team writes given-when-then scenarios for a password reset so the product owner can confirm the expected behaviour before developers automate those scenarios.$L$
