select c.id, $L$m2-11$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is a recognized risk or limitation of relying on DevOps and heavy test automation?$L$, $J$[{"text":"It may require significant setup and can shift, rather than remove, the need for skilled testing","correct":true,"why":"DevOps demands tooling investment and skilled people; automation supports but does not replace human testing insight."},{"text":"It makes all manual and exploratory testing pointless","correct":false,"why":"Exploratory and other human testing remain valuable; automation cannot cover everything."},{"text":"It guarantees defect-free releases","correct":false,"why":"No approach guarantees defect-free software; DevOps reduces but cannot remove risk."},{"text":"It prevents any feedback from reaching developers","correct":false,"why":"The opposite is true: DevOps improves and speeds developer feedback."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$While DevOps improves feedback and consistency, it introduces setup and tooling costs and still depends on skilled testers for activities automation cannot cover, such as exploratory testing. Recognizing both benefits and risks is part of understanding DevOps and testing.$L$, $L$A startup adopts DevOps but still schedules exploratory test sessions each release, because automated checks missed a confusing but technically valid checkout flow.$L$
