select c.id, $L$m2-14$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$Which test level focuses on testing individual components or modules in isolation?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Component (unit) testing","correct":true,"why":"Component testing verifies individual units or modules separately, often by developers, against their detailed design."},{"text":"System testing","correct":false,"why":"System testing evaluates the whole integrated system, not isolated units."},{"text":"Acceptance testing","correct":false,"why":"Acceptance testing validates fitness for use by the business, not isolated components."},{"text":"Integration testing","correct":false,"why":"Integration testing checks interactions between components, not a single component alone."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Component (unit) testing is the test level that examines individual modules in isolation, typically using the detailed design or code as its test basis. Distinguishing the objectives and test basis of each level is core to the SDLC syllabus.$L$, $L$A developer writes unit tests for a single date-parsing function, mocking its dependencies so only that function's logic is exercised.$L$
