select c.id, $L$m2-15$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$What is the primary objective of integration testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"To expose defects in the interfaces and interactions between integrated components or systems","correct":true,"why":"Integration testing targets the interfaces and data exchange between parts, where component testing cannot reach."},{"text":"To confirm the system meets business needs for release","correct":false,"why":"That is the objective of acceptance testing, not integration testing."},{"text":"To test a single component fully in isolation","correct":false,"why":"Isolated single-component testing is component testing, not integration testing."},{"text":"To measure only the response time of the whole system","correct":false,"why":"Response time is a non-functional concern typically evaluated at system testing."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Integration testing concentrates on the interfaces and interactions between components (component integration) or between systems (system integration), using interface and architectural specifications as its test basis. Its objective differs from testing components alone or the whole system.$L$, $L$After unit-testing the payment module and the order module separately, the team tests that an order correctly triggers and receives a payment confirmation across the two.$L$
