select c.id, $L$m2-16$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is the typical test basis for system testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"System and software requirement specifications and use cases","correct":true,"why":"System testing verifies end-to-end behaviour against system-level requirements and specified behaviour."},{"text":"The detailed low-level design of a single class","correct":false,"why":"Detailed design of one unit is the basis for component testing, not system testing."},{"text":"Only the user's informal verbal expectations","correct":false,"why":"Acceptance testing may lean on user needs, but system testing uses specified requirements."},{"text":"The database index configuration file","correct":false,"why":"A single configuration file is not the defined test basis for system-level behaviour."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$System testing evaluates the behaviour of the whole integrated system, using system and software requirement specifications, use cases, and risk analyses as its test basis. Knowing the test basis and test object for each level is central to this syllabus topic.$L$, $L$The team runs end-to-end scenarios for an insurance quote system against the documented system requirements, covering the full quote-to-policy flow in a production-like environment.$L$
