select c.id, $L$m2-18$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following best describes functional testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Evaluating what the system does against specified functional requirements","correct":true,"why":"Functional testing checks the functions the system should perform, based on functional requirements."},{"text":"Evaluating how well the system performs, such as speed and capacity","correct":false,"why":"That describes non-functional testing, which addresses quality characteristics like performance."},{"text":"Examining internal code structure to derive test cases","correct":false,"why":"That is white-box (structure-based) testing, a technique category, not functional testing."},{"text":"Testing only after the system is retired from service","correct":false,"why":"Functional testing occurs during development and maintenance, not after retirement."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Functional testing assesses what the system does, verifying behaviour against functional requirements and specifications. It is contrasted with non-functional testing and with structure-based (white-box) approaches in the test types section of the syllabus.$L$, $L$A tester verifies that a search feature returns the correct products for various keywords, confirming the function behaves as the requirements state.$L$
