select c.id, $L$m2-19$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is an example of non-functional testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Performance testing that measures response time under expected load","correct":true,"why":"Performance is a quality characteristic, so measuring response under load is non-functional testing."},{"text":"Verifying that a login accepts valid credentials","correct":false,"why":"Checking correct login behaviour is functional testing of what the system does."},{"text":"Checking that a calculation returns the right total","correct":false,"why":"Confirming correct results is functional testing, not a quality-characteristic test."},{"text":"Confirming a menu item opens the correct screen","correct":false,"why":"Navigation to the correct screen is functional behaviour, not a non-functional attribute."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Non-functional testing evaluates quality characteristics such as performance, usability, reliability, and security, describing how well the system behaves rather than what it does. Performance testing under load is a classic non-functional example from the test types syllabus area.$L$, $L$Before a ticket-sales launch, the team runs a load test simulating 10,000 concurrent buyers to confirm the site stays responsive under peak demand.$L$
