select c.id, $L$m2-20$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$White-box (structure-based) testing derives test cases primarily from which source?$L$, $J$[{"text":"The internal structure or implementation of the test object, such as code and control flow","correct":true,"why":"White-box testing uses knowledge of internal structure, like code and paths, to design and measure tests."},{"text":"Only the external requirements, with no knowledge of the code","correct":false,"why":"Deriving tests solely from external behaviour is black-box testing."},{"text":"User complaints gathered after release","correct":false,"why":"Post-release complaints are not the structural basis for white-box test design."},{"text":"The marketing brochure for the product","correct":false,"why":"A brochure is not a technical basis for structure-based test derivation."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$White-box testing is based on the internal structure of the test object, such as code, control flow, and architecture, and can measure structural coverage. It contrasts with black-box testing, which is based on external behaviour, in the test types syllabus content.$L$, $L$A developer inspects the branches of a pricing algorithm and designs tests to ensure every decision path, including the rarely hit discount branch, is executed at least once.$L$
