select c.id, $L$m2-21$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which pair correctly matches the testing type to its basis?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Black-box testing is based on external behaviour; white-box testing is based on internal structure","correct":true,"why":"Black-box derives tests from specifications and behaviour, while white-box derives them from internal structure."},{"text":"Black-box testing is based on source code; white-box testing is based on requirements","correct":false,"why":"This reverses the definitions; black-box uses behaviour, white-box uses code."},{"text":"Both black-box and white-box testing are based only on the source code","correct":false,"why":"Black-box does not require code knowledge; it works from external behaviour."},{"text":"Both are based only on user manuals","correct":false,"why":"White-box specifically relies on internal structure, not user manuals."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Black-box (behaviour-based) testing designs tests from specifications and external behaviour, whereas white-box (structure-based) testing designs and measures tests from internal structure. Correctly distinguishing these is a core objective of the test types syllabus area.$L$, $L$A tester uses black-box equivalence classes to check a form's validation from the outside, while a developer uses white-box coverage to ensure each validation branch executes.$L$
