select c.id, $L$m2-22$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$A defect was fixed in the checkout module. Running the previously failing test again to verify the fix is an example of which activity?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Confirmation testing","correct":true,"why":"Confirmation testing re-runs the tests that failed to confirm the original defect is now resolved."},{"text":"Regression testing","correct":false,"why":"Regression testing checks that the fix has not broken other, previously working areas."},{"text":"System testing","correct":false,"why":"System testing is a test level; the activity described is specifically re-testing a fix."},{"text":"Load testing","correct":false,"why":"Load testing evaluates performance under load, unrelated to verifying a specific fix."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Confirmation testing (re-testing) executes the test cases that previously failed to confirm that the defect has been successfully fixed. It is distinct from regression testing, which looks for unintended side effects elsewhere.$L$, $L$After developers patch a bug where discount codes were ignored, the tester re-runs the exact failing scenario and confirms the discount now applies correctly.$L$
