select c.id, $L$m2-24$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$What is maintenance testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Testing performed on an existing operational system after changes, migration, or retirement","correct":true,"why":"Maintenance testing evaluates changes to a system in operation and the impact of those changes on the unchanged parts."},{"text":"Testing done only before a system is first released","correct":false,"why":"That is initial development testing; maintenance testing occurs after the system is in operation."},{"text":"A synonym for component testing","correct":false,"why":"Component testing is a test level; maintenance testing is triggered by changes to a live system."},{"text":"Testing that is only ever performed manually","correct":false,"why":"Maintenance testing can be manual or automated; the defining trait is that it follows changes to an operational system."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Maintenance testing is carried out on an existing operational system whenever it is modified, migrated, or retired, and includes both testing the change and regression testing the parts that were not changed. Its scope depends on the risk and size of the change.$L$, $L$After a live payroll system is patched for a new tax rule, the team tests the new rule and regression-tests existing pay calculations to ensure nothing else broke.$L$
