select c.id, $L$m2-25$L$, $L$Software Development Lifecycle$L$, 2, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is a typical trigger for maintenance testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Migration of the operational system to a new platform or environment","correct":true,"why":"Migration is a recognized maintenance trigger, requiring operational and conversion testing on the moved system."},{"text":"Writing the first line of code for a brand-new product","correct":false,"why":"Initial development is not maintenance; maintenance applies to systems already in operation."},{"text":"Choosing which SDLC model to adopt for a new project","correct":false,"why":"Selecting an SDLC model is a planning decision, not a maintenance-testing trigger."},{"text":"Drafting the original requirements specification","correct":false,"why":"Initial requirements work precedes operation; maintenance testing follows changes to a live system."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Maintenance testing is triggered by modifications such as enhancements and corrective fixes, by environment changes like migration or upgrades, and by planned retirement of a system. Recognizing these triggers is part of understanding maintenance testing in the SDLC syllabus.$L$, $L$When an insurer moves its policy system from on-premise servers to the cloud, the team runs maintenance tests to confirm the migrated system still processes claims correctly.$L$
