select c.id, $L$m3-07$L$, $L$Static Testing$L$, 3, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which statement about the relationship between static and dynamic testing is TRUE?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Static testing finds defects directly, while dynamic testing observes failures caused by defects","correct":true,"why":"Static testing locates the defect itself in the work product; dynamic testing sees a failure and the defect must then be traced."},{"text":"Both static and dynamic testing require executing the software","correct":false,"why":"Only dynamic testing executes the software."},{"text":"Static testing can only be done manually, never with tools","correct":false,"why":"Static analysis tools support static testing without human execution of code."},{"text":"Dynamic testing directly identifies the exact line of code that is defective","correct":false,"why":"Dynamic testing reveals a failure; locating the causing defect requires further debugging."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$In static testing the defect is identified directly. In dynamic testing a failure is caused by a defect when the code runs, and additional analysis is needed to find the underlying defect.$L$, $L$A reviewer points at the exact faulty condition in the code, whereas a failing test only shows the wrong output on screen until a developer debugs it.$L$
