select c.id, $L$m3-08$L$, $L$Static Testing$L$, 3, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$In the context of static testing, what is the primary purpose of feedback from reviews?$L$, $J$[{"text":"To provide early, frequent feedback on quality problems so they can be addressed promptly","correct":true,"why":"Frequent early feedback is a core value of static testing, enabling fast correction and process improvement."},{"text":"To assign blame for defects to individual authors","correct":false,"why":"Reviews focus on the work product, not on blaming people."},{"text":"To replace the need for stakeholder communication","correct":false,"why":"Feedback improves communication rather than removing the need for it."},{"text":"To measure the execution speed of the software","correct":false,"why":"Execution speed is unrelated to static feedback and requires dynamic testing."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Static testing enables early and frequent feedback, allowing quality problems to be identified and corrected quickly and helping the team learn and improve its process.$L$, $L$Frequent pull-request reviews give developers quick feedback, so recurring mistakes get corrected before they become team-wide habits.$L$
