select c.id, $L$m3-23$L$, $L$Static Testing$L$, 3, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is a recognized success factor for reviews?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Choosing the review type and techniques suitable for the objectives, type of work product, and participants","correct":true,"why":"Fitting the review approach to the objectives and context is an organizational success factor for reviews."},{"text":"Ensuring reviews always find the maximum possible number of defects regardless of effort","correct":false,"why":"Reviews should be efficient and purpose-driven, not maximize defect counts at any cost."},{"text":"Focusing feedback on the personality of the author","correct":false,"why":"Reviews should focus on the work product, not on the person, to keep them constructive."},{"text":"Keeping the review objectives secret from participants","correct":false,"why":"Clear, shared objectives are needed; hiding them undermines the review."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Success factors include having clear objectives, choosing the appropriate review type, conducting reviews on small chunks, giving feedback constructively, and recognizing the effort as part of process improvement.$L$, $L$A lead picks a lightweight walkthrough for a small script but a full inspection for a critical interface spec, matching the review type to the risk.$L$
