select c.id, $L$m4-22$L$, $L$Test Analysis & Design Techniques$L$, 4, $L$K3$L$, null, null, $L$A component contains 8 branch outcomes (4 decisions, each with a true and false outcome). A test suite exercises 6 of these outcomes. What branch coverage has been achieved?$L$, $J$[{"text":"75%.","correct":true,"why":"Branch coverage = outcomes exercised / total outcomes = 6/8 = 75%."},{"text":"50%.","correct":false,"why":"6 of 8 is 75%; 50% would be 4 of 8."},{"text":"60%.","correct":false,"why":"6/8 is 75%, not 60%; 60% would be 6 of 10."},{"text":"100%.","correct":false,"why":"Two of the eight outcomes are unexercised, so coverage is below 100%."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Branch coverage counts decision outcomes, not decisions. With 4 decisions there are 8 outcomes; exercising 6 gives 6/8 = 75%.$L$, $L$A CI gate reports 75% branch coverage for a module; the tester identifies which two outcomes (both false branches of the last two if statements) are missing and adds cases to reach 100%.$L$
