select c.id, $L$m5-13$L$, $L$Managing the Test Process$L$, 5, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following best describes requirements-based test case prioritisation?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Ordering test cases according to the priority of the requirements they verify.","correct":true,"why":"Requirements-based prioritisation follows the importance assigned to the requirements each test covers."},{"text":"Ordering test cases by the length of their test steps.","correct":false,"why":"Test step length is unrelated to requirement priority."},{"text":"Ordering test cases to maximise code coverage as fast as possible.","correct":false,"why":"That describes coverage-based prioritisation, not requirements-based."},{"text":"Ordering test cases so that automated tests always run before manual tests.","correct":false,"why":"Automation status is not the basis for requirements-based prioritisation."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Requirements-based prioritisation sequences test cases according to the priority of the requirements they cover, so that tests verifying the most important requirements run first.$L$, $L$The product owner marks three requirements as must-have and five as nice-to-have; the tester schedules the must-have requirement tests at the start of the cycle.$L$
