select c.id, $L$m6-06$L$, $L$Test Management$L$, 6, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$A stakeholder asks how much trust the team has that the product is ready for release. Which type of metric best answers this?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Confidence metrics","correct":true,"why":"Confidence metrics capture the degree of trust stakeholders have in the product, often informed by coverage and defect trends."},{"text":"Coverage metrics only","correct":false,"why":"Coverage contributes to confidence but by itself does not express stakeholder trust in readiness."},{"text":"Effort and cost metrics","correct":false,"why":"Cost and effort track resource usage, not the confidence in product quality."},{"text":"Environment availability metrics","correct":false,"why":"Environment availability is a logistical status, not a measure of trust in the product."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Confidence metrics express how much trust stakeholders place in the product or in the testing performed. They are often derived from other metrics such as coverage achieved and defect trends.$L$, $L$Before a go/no-go meeting the team summarizes high requirement coverage and a declining defect discovery rate to argue that confidence in the release is high.$L$
