select c.id, $L$m6-14$L$, $L$Test Management$L$, 6, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Why does configuration management need to be in place before testing begins in earnest?$L$, $J$[{"text":"So that all test items and testware are uniquely identified and traceable throughout the test process","correct":true,"why":"Establishing configuration management up front ensures items and testware are version controlled from the start, keeping results traceable and reproducible."},{"text":"So that testers do not need to write any test cases","correct":false,"why":"Configuration management does not remove the need to design tests; it controls versions of the work products."},{"text":"So that defects are automatically corrected by the tool","correct":false,"why":"Configuration management tracks versions; it does not fix defects automatically."},{"text":"So that the project no longer needs a test plan","correct":false,"why":"A test plan is still required; configuration management complements it rather than replacing it."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$The ISTQB syllabus stresses that configuration management should be established before testing begins so that all items and testware are identified and version controlled, supporting traceability of the test basis and results.$L$, $L$The team sets up version control for scripts, test data and environment definitions in sprint zero, so from the first real test run everything is traceable to a known baseline.$L$
