select c.id, $L$m7-12$L$, $L$Defect Management$L$, 7, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is a valid source of a defect report arising from STATIC testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"A reviewer finds an ambiguous, testable-but-contradictory requirement during a requirements review","correct":true,"why":"Static testing examines work products without executing code, so defects in requirements, designs, or documents (for example ambiguities or contradictions) are found and reported this way."},{"text":"A test script throws an exception when executed against the running application","correct":false,"why":"An exception during execution is a dynamic testing finding because the software was run to observe the failure."},{"text":"A load test reveals the server slows down under 5000 concurrent users","correct":false,"why":"Measuring behaviour under load requires executing the system, which is dynamic, not static, testing."},{"text":"A user reports the mobile app crashes on launch in production","correct":false,"why":"A crash observed by running the app is a dynamic/operational failure, not a static review finding."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Static testing (reviews and static analysis) finds defects in work products without executing code, such as requirement ambiguities, design flaws, or coding standard violations. Dynamic testing finds failures by running the software.$L$, $L$In a requirements walkthrough a reviewer spots that two acceptance criteria contradict each other and raises a defect against the specification before a single line of code is written.$L$
