select c.id, $L$m7-15$L$, $L$Defect Management$L$, 7, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$During defect triage, whose input is MOST appropriate for deciding the priority (fix order) of a defect?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Product owner or business stakeholder input, informed by developer effort and tester impact assessment","correct":true,"why":"Priority is a business decision about urgency and order of fixing, best set by product/business stakeholders using technical input; severity is more a technical impact judgement."},{"text":"The tester alone, without any business or development input","correct":false,"why":"A tester can assess severity/impact but priority requires business context on urgency and value that the tester may not hold alone."},{"text":"A random selection to avoid bias","correct":false,"why":"Prioritisation should be a deliberate risk- and value-based decision, not arbitrary."},{"text":"Whoever shouts loudest in the meeting","correct":false,"why":"Priority must be justified by impact, risk, and business value, not by who is most vocal."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Priority reflects the business urgency of fixing a defect, so it is best decided with product/business stakeholders using technical impact (severity) and effort information from testers and developers.$L$, $L$In sprint triage the product owner bumps a checkout bug above a reporting bug because it blocks revenue, after the tester confirms impact and the developer estimates the fix.$L$
