select c.id, $L$m9-02$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is the BEST example of a test activity that tool support makes practical when it would be nearly impossible manually?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Simulating thousands of concurrent users to measure performance under load","correct":true,"why":"Generating and coordinating thousands of virtual users is impractical by hand, so performance tools are essential for this activity."},{"text":"Deciding which risks are most important to the business","correct":false,"why":"Prioritising business risk is a human judgement activity, not something a tool performs for you."},{"text":"Reviewing a requirements document for ambiguous wording","correct":false,"why":"Understanding ambiguous natural language is a human review skill; tools assist but cannot replace the reviewer's judgement."},{"text":"Choosing an appropriate test design technique for a feature","correct":false,"why":"Selecting techniques relies on tester analysis and experience rather than automated tooling."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Some activities are simply not feasible manually - generating load from thousands of simultaneous users is the textbook example. Tools shine where volume, repetition or precise measurement exceed human capacity, whereas judgement-heavy activities stay with people.$L$, $L$Before a Black Friday sale, an e-commerce team uses a load tool to simulate 20,000 concurrent shoppers. No manual team could reproduce that traffic, so the tool is the only realistic way to expose the slow checkout under peak load.$L$
