select c.id, $L$m9-04$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$A tool examines source code for coding-standard violations and potential defects without running the program. Into which category does this tool fall?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Static testing tools (static analysis)","correct":true,"why":"Analysing code without executing it, to find violations and potential defects, is exactly what static analysis tools do."},{"text":"Test execution tools","correct":false,"why":"Execution tools run tests against a running system; this tool does not execute the program."},{"text":"Coverage measurement tools","correct":false,"why":"Coverage tools measure which parts of code were exercised during dynamic execution, not standards compliance without running."},{"text":"Monitoring tools","correct":false,"why":"Monitoring tools observe a running system in operation, not static source examination."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Static analysis tools inspect code and other artefacts without execution, flagging standards violations, complexity issues, security weaknesses and suspicious constructs. Because they run early, they catch defects cheaply before code is ever executed.$L$, $L$A developer commits code and a static analysis tool immediately flags an unused variable and a potential null-pointer path. The issue is fixed in minutes, long before any test is executed against a build.$L$
