select c.id, $L$m9-06$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$During dynamic test execution a tool reports that 78% of the code statements were exercised by the test suite. Which category of tool produced this figure?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Coverage measurement tools","correct":true,"why":"Coverage tools instrument code and measure which statements, branches or paths were exercised during execution."},{"text":"Static analysis tools","correct":false,"why":"Static analysis does not execute code, so it cannot report exercised statements."},{"text":"Test management tools","correct":false,"why":"Management tools track the process; they do not instrument code to measure coverage."},{"text":"Performance testing tools","correct":false,"why":"Performance tools measure response and load behaviour, not structural coverage."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Coverage tools measure the degree to which code structures (statements, branches, decisions) are exercised by tests during execution. This helps a team see untested areas, though high coverage alone never proves the tests are meaningful.$L$, $L$After a test run, a coverage tool shows an error-handling block was never executed. The team adds a negative test to reach it and discovers the block actually logs to the wrong file - a defect that would otherwise have shipped.$L$
