select c.id, $L$m9-07$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$Which category of tool observes a system in operation and raises alerts when metrics such as response time, memory, or error rates exceed thresholds?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Monitoring tools","correct":true,"why":"Monitoring tools continuously observe a running system and alert when defined thresholds are breached."},{"text":"Test design tools","correct":false,"why":"Test design tools help derive test cases from a basis, not observe a running system."},{"text":"Static analysis tools","correct":false,"why":"Static analysis does not observe a running system; it inspects artefacts without execution."},{"text":"Test data preparation tools","correct":false,"why":"Data preparation tools provision inputs; they do not monitor a live system's metrics."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Monitoring tools watch live or test systems and report on resource use, throughput, response times and errors, often raising alerts. They are closely related to performance tooling and are important for operational and reliability testing.$L$, $L$A monitoring tool alerts an on-call tester that API error rates jumped to 4% after a deploy. The team rolls back within minutes, well before most users notice - the alert turned a potential outage into a non-event.$L$
