select c.id, $L$m9-08$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following tools is MOST directly associated with a DevOps / continuous integration approach to testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"A pipeline tool that automatically builds the software and triggers automated tests on every code commit","correct":true,"why":"CI tools automatically integrate, build and test on each commit, which is central to DevOps delivery."},{"text":"A spreadsheet used to record manual exploratory session notes","correct":false,"why":"A manual notes spreadsheet is not a CI/DevOps automation tool."},{"text":"A tool that only masks personal data in a database","correct":false,"why":"Data masking is a data-preparation activity, not the defining tool of a CI pipeline."},{"text":"A whiteboard used during a risk workshop","correct":false,"why":"A whiteboard supports human collaboration, not automated continuous integration."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Continuous integration and DevOps toolchains automatically build and test software whenever code changes, giving fast feedback. Automated tests wired into the pipeline are what make continuous integration deliver value.$L$, $L$Every time a developer pushes code, the CI server builds the app and runs the unit and API test suites. A broken login flow is caught within eight minutes of the commit, so the developer fixes it while the context is still fresh.$L$
