select c.id, $L$m9-09$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following is a genuine BENEFIT of test automation as described by ISTQB?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Reduction of repetitive manual work, freeing testers for activities that need human insight","correct":true,"why":"Automating repetitive execution reduces tedious manual effort and lets testers focus on judgement-based work."},{"text":"Complete elimination of the need for any test maintenance","correct":false,"why":"Automated tests require ongoing maintenance; automation does not remove that need - it adds it."},{"text":"A guarantee that no defects will reach production","correct":false,"why":"No automation can guarantee zero defects; that is an unrealistic expectation."},{"text":"Removal of the need for testers to understand the system under test","correct":false,"why":"Automation still requires deep understanding to design and interpret the tests correctly."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Real benefits of automation include less repetitive manual effort, greater consistency and repeatability, faster feedback, better coverage of certain areas, and objective measurement. These are concrete gains - not promises of perfection.$L$, $L$After automating the nightly regression suite, a team's manual testers stop spending Mondays re-running the same checks and instead do exploratory testing on new features, finding subtle usability defects the scripts would never catch.$L$
