select c.id, $L$m9-19$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$In a CI/CD pipeline, when are automated tests typically triggered?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Automatically, when code is committed or integrated into the shared codebase","correct":true,"why":"Continuous integration runs automated builds and tests on each commit or integration, giving rapid feedback."},{"text":"Only once, manually, at the very end of the project","correct":false,"why":"That describes late manual testing, the opposite of continuous integration's frequent automated runs."},{"text":"Only when a customer reports a defect in production","correct":false,"why":"CI runs proactively on changes, not reactively only after production defects."},{"text":"Never - CI pipelines do not run tests","correct":false,"why":"Running automated tests is a core purpose of a CI pipeline."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$In continuous integration, committing code triggers an automated build followed by automated tests. This gives fast feedback so integration problems are caught early, while the change is still fresh in the developer's mind.$L$, $L$A developer merges a branch at 2pm; by 2:07pm the pipeline has built the app and reported a failing unit test. The developer fixes it before leaving for the day, avoiding a bug that would otherwise surface a week later in system testing.$L$
