select c.id, $L$m9-20$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$What is a primary benefit of wiring automated tests into a CI/CD pipeline at the foundation level?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Fast, frequent feedback on the impact of code changes, so defects are found soon after they are introduced","correct":true,"why":"Automated tests on every change provide rapid feedback, enabling early detection close to when defects are introduced."},{"text":"It removes the need for any test design or planning","correct":false,"why":"CI still relies on well-designed tests; the pipeline runs them, it does not design them."},{"text":"It guarantees that the released software has zero defects","correct":false,"why":"No pipeline can guarantee zero defects; it improves feedback speed, not perfection."},{"text":"It eliminates the need for developers to write code carefully","correct":false,"why":"Fast feedback supports careful development; it does not excuse poor coding."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$The value of automation in CI/CD is speed and frequency of feedback. Because tests run on every integration, defects surface early and cheaply, integration risk stays low, and the team can release changes with greater confidence.$L$, $L$A team releases small changes several times a day. Because every change is auto-tested in the pipeline, a regression in the pricing rule is caught within minutes of being introduced, not discovered by a customer weeks later.$L$
