select c.id, $L$m9-21$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which of the following BEST describes the relationship between automated tests and manual testing in a mature test approach?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Automation handles repeatable, high-volume checks while manual testing focuses on exploration and human judgement","correct":true,"why":"Automation and manual testing are complementary: each is suited to different tasks, and both are needed."},{"text":"Automation should always completely replace manual testing","correct":false,"why":"Full replacement causes over-reliance and misses defects only humans notice."},{"text":"Manual testing should always completely replace automation","correct":false,"why":"That discards automation's real benefits in speed, consistency and volume."},{"text":"The two are interchangeable and it never matters which you use","correct":false,"why":"They have different strengths, so the choice does matter for effectiveness."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Automation and manual testing are complementary. Automation excels at repeatable, high-volume, precise checks; manual and exploratory testing excel at judgement, usability and the unexpected. A balanced approach uses each for what it does best.$L$, $L$A team automates its 400-check regression suite for speed and consistency, but keeps exploratory sessions for each new feature. The scripts guard against regressions while the human sessions catch the confusing workflows automation would never question.$L$
