select c.id, $L$m9-25$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which category of tool helps testers systematically derive test cases or generate expected results from a specified test basis such as a model or set of rules?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Test design tools","correct":true,"why":"Test design tools support deriving test cases, and sometimes expected results, from a test basis such as requirements or models."},{"text":"Monitoring tools","correct":false,"why":"Monitoring tools observe a running system's metrics; they do not derive test cases from a basis."},{"text":"Defect management tools","correct":false,"why":"Defect tools track reported defects; they do not generate test cases from a test basis."},{"text":"Performance testing tools","correct":false,"why":"Performance tools generate load and measure behaviour, not derive test cases from a specification."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Test design tools support the creation of test cases (and sometimes expected results) from a test basis such as requirements, models or interfaces. They help apply techniques consistently and can improve coverage of the specified conditions.$L$, $L$Given a decision table of business rules, a test design tool generates the full set of rule combinations as draft test cases. The tester reviews and refines them, ensuring no rule combination is accidentally left untested.$L$
