select c.id, $L$m10-06$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Which statement best describes a tester's mindset on an agile team?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Curious, collaborative and quality-focused, providing rapid feedback throughout the iteration","correct":true,"why":"Agile testers work closely with the team, question assumptions and give fast feedback so the increment stays on quality track."},{"text":"A gatekeeper who works in isolation and only reports at the end","correct":false,"why":"Working in isolation and testing only at the end is contrary to agile ways of working."},{"text":"Someone who avoids talking to developers to stay independent","correct":false,"why":"Independence in agile does not mean avoiding communication; collaboration is essential."},{"text":"A role that only executes scripted tests written months in advance","correct":false,"why":"Agile testing relies heavily on adaptable, exploratory and just-in-time test design, not only long-dated scripts."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$An agile tester is collaborative and communicative, brings a questioning and quality-focused mindset, and provides continuous, rapid feedback. This differs from a traditional isolated end-of-cycle gatekeeper role.$L$, $L$During a sprint the tester pairs with a developer, raises questions about an unclear rule immediately, and demonstrates a failing scenario the same day rather than logging it for a later phase.$L$
