select c.id, $L$m10-07$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$On an agile team, which activities is a tester likely to be involved in beyond executing tests?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Clarifying user stories, defining acceptance criteria and helping automate tests","correct":true,"why":"Agile testers contribute across the lifecycle, including refining stories, shaping acceptance criteria and supporting test automation."},{"text":"Only running a final regression pass before release and nothing else","correct":false,"why":"That is a narrow, phase-based view that does not reflect the agile tester's broader involvement."},{"text":"Writing the production code for every feature","correct":false,"why":"Testers may pair with developers, but writing all production code is not their role."},{"text":"Approving the budget and staffing for the project","correct":false,"why":"Budget and staffing are management responsibilities, not testing tasks."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Agile testers participate throughout the iteration: helping to define and clarify acceptance criteria, contributing to backlog refinement, designing and executing tests, and supporting automation. Their role is broad and collaborative.$L$, $L$In backlog refinement the tester spots a missing acceptance criterion for an error case, and the team adds it before the story is pulled into a sprint.$L$
