select c.id, $L$m10-09$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$How does test automation support testing in an agile team working in short iterations?$L$, $J$[{"text":"It runs regression checks quickly and repeatedly, freeing testers for exploratory and new-feature testing","correct":true,"why":"Automated regression provides fast, repeatable feedback so people can focus on judgement-based and new-feature testing each iteration."},{"text":"It means manual and exploratory testing are no longer needed","correct":false,"why":"Automation handles repetitive checks but does not replace human exploratory testing."},{"text":"It removes the need to maintain any tests over time","correct":false,"why":"Automated tests require ongoing maintenance as the product changes."},{"text":"It guarantees the product has no defects once the suite passes green","correct":false,"why":"A passing suite reduces risk but never guarantees a defect-free product."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Automation is central to agile testing because short iterations demand frequent regression checking. Automating repetitive regression tests gives fast feedback and lets testers spend their time on exploratory testing and testing new features, though automation still needs maintenance.$L$, $L$The team automates its core regression suite so it runs on every build overnight, leaving the tester free to explore the new features added during the sprint.$L$
