select c.id, $L$m10-14$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$From a testing perspective, how does release planning differ from iteration planning?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Release planning looks further ahead across multiple iterations, helping testers anticipate broader test and regression needs","correct":true,"why":"Release planning takes a longer horizon, so testers can foresee end-to-end and regression scope spanning several iterations."},{"text":"Release planning is identical to iteration planning with a different name","correct":false,"why":"They operate at different horizons and levels of detail."},{"text":"Release planning replaces the need for iteration planning","correct":false,"why":"Both coexist; each serves a different planning horizon."},{"text":"Release planning never involves testers","correct":false,"why":"Testers contribute to release planning to inform release-level test and risk considerations."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Release planning looks ahead across several iterations to shape the overall release, while iteration planning focuses on the immediate iteration. Testers use release planning to anticipate broader concerns such as end-to-end testing and cumulative regression scope.$L$, $L$At release planning the tester highlights that a large cross-cutting feature will need a coordinated end-to-end test near the end of the release, so time is reserved for it.$L$
