select c.id, $L$m10-15$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$What does independence of testing provide, even when testing is embedded in an agile team?$L$, $J$[{"text":"A fresh, less biased perspective that can find defects the author might overlook","correct":true,"why":"Independent eyes bring different assumptions, so they detect failures and false assumptions the original author may miss."},{"text":"A guarantee that testers will find every defect","correct":false,"why":"Independence improves defect detection but never guarantees finding all defects."},{"text":"Proof that the developers wrote poor-quality code","correct":false,"why":"Independent testing is about perspective, not an accusation about code quality."},{"text":"The ability to skip involving developers entirely","correct":false,"why":"Independence does not mean cutting off collaboration with developers."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Independence of testing brings a different viewpoint and reduces author bias, helping to reveal defects and incorrect assumptions. This benefit applies even when a tester is a full member of an agile team.$L$, $L$A tester questions an assumption the developer took for granted about how dates roll over at year end, uncovering a defect the developer had not considered.$L$
