select c.id, $L$m10-16$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$What is a recognised drawback of relying solely on developers to test their own work in an agile team?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Author bias can make people less likely to spot problems in their own work","correct":true,"why":"People tend to be blind to their own assumptions and mistakes, so self-testing alone can miss defects."},{"text":"Developers are technically incapable of writing any tests","correct":false,"why":"Developers can and do write tests; the issue is bias, not capability."},{"text":"It always makes testing faster and more thorough","correct":false,"why":"Self-testing alone can reduce thoroughness because of bias, not increase it."},{"text":"It removes all need for automation","correct":false,"why":"The point concerns independence of perspective, not automation."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$A drawback of testing only by the author is author bias: it is hard to see one's own errors and assumptions. This is why some degree of independent testing is valuable even within a collaborative agile team.$L$, $L$A developer's unit tests all pass because they mirror the same misunderstanding in the code, and only an independent tester exercising the requirement uncovers the gap.$L$
