select c.id, $L$m10-19$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$What does continuous delivery (CD) require in order to release changes safely and frequently?$L$, $J$[{"text":"A high level of automated testing so each change can be validated quickly and reliably","correct":true,"why":"Frequent, safe releases depend on automated tests giving trustworthy, fast confirmation that changes are sound."},{"text":"A long manual test phase before every release","correct":false,"why":"A long manual gate would prevent the frequent, fast releases CD aims for."},{"text":"Removing testing from the pipeline to speed things up","correct":false,"why":"CD increases reliance on automated testing rather than removing it."},{"text":"Releasing only once the whole product is complete","correct":false,"why":"CD is about releasing changes frequently, not waiting for a finished product."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Continuous delivery aims to keep software in a releasable state so changes can be delivered frequently and safely. This depends heavily on extensive, reliable automated testing in the pipeline to validate each change quickly.$L$, $L$Because the pipeline runs a trusted automated test suite on every change, the team can release small updates several times a week with confidence.$L$
