select c.id, $L$m10-20$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$What is the purpose of confirmation testing (re-testing) after a defect is fixed?$L$, $J$[{"text":"To confirm that the original defect has actually been resolved","correct":true,"why":"Confirmation testing re-runs the failing test on the fixed build to verify the defect no longer occurs."},{"text":"To check that unrelated areas still work after the change","correct":false,"why":"That describes regression testing, not confirmation testing."},{"text":"To measure how fast the system responds under load","correct":false,"why":"That is performance testing, unrelated to confirming a fix."},{"text":"To gather new requirements for the next iteration","correct":false,"why":"Requirements gathering is not a testing activity of this kind."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Confirmation testing (re-testing) verifies that a previously failing test now passes after the corresponding defect has been fixed. It confirms the specific fix worked.$L$, $L$After a developer fixes a rounding error in an invoice total, the tester re-runs the exact scenario that failed to confirm the total is now correct.$L$
