select c.id, $L$m10-21$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K1$L$, null, null, $L$What is the purpose of regression testing when changes are made in an iteration?$L$, $J$[{"text":"To detect whether the changes have unintentionally broken previously working functionality","correct":true,"why":"Regression testing checks that existing features still work after code has changed."},{"text":"To confirm that a specific fixed defect is now resolved","correct":false,"why":"That is confirmation testing, which targets the specific fix."},{"text":"To define the acceptance criteria for a new story","correct":false,"why":"Defining acceptance criteria is a planning activity, not regression testing."},{"text":"To measure code coverage of unit tests only","correct":false,"why":"Coverage measurement is a different concern from regression testing."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Regression testing aims to find unintended side effects, verifying that changes such as fixes or new features have not broken existing functionality. In agile, frequent changes make regression testing a constant need.$L$, $L$After adding a new discount type, the tester runs the regression suite to make sure existing pricing and checkout behaviour is unaffected.$L$
