select c.id, $L$m10-22$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$Why is regression testing under particular pressure in short agile iterations?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Frequent changes each iteration mean the regression scope keeps growing while the time available stays short","correct":true,"why":"Every iteration adds functionality that must keep working, so the regression burden accumulates against a fixed, short timebox."},{"text":"Because regression testing is never needed in agile","correct":false,"why":"Regression testing is more, not less, important in agile due to frequent change."},{"text":"Because agile forbids automating regression tests","correct":false,"why":"Agile actively encourages automating regression tests to cope with the pressure."},{"text":"Because requirements never change, making regression trivial","correct":false,"why":"Requirements do change in agile, which is exactly why regression pressure grows."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Because agile delivers changes every iteration, the body of functionality that must be re-verified grows continually while the iteration timebox stays short. This creates strong pressure to automate regression testing so it can keep pace.$L$, $L$By sprint eight the manual regression checklist is too large to run by hand each sprint, so the team invests in automating the most critical regression cases.$L$
