select c.id, $L$m10-23$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, null, null, $L$How does automating the regression suite help a team cope with short iterations?$L$, $J$[{"text":"It lets the growing set of regression tests run quickly and often, keeping feedback fast as functionality accumulates","correct":true,"why":"Automation runs the accumulating regression tests rapidly and repeatedly, so the team keeps fast feedback despite the short timebox."},{"text":"It permanently removes the need for confirmation testing","correct":false,"why":"Confirmation testing of specific fixes is still required regardless of regression automation."},{"text":"It means new features never need any testing","correct":false,"why":"New features still require fresh testing; automation targets repeatable regression checks."},{"text":"It ensures the regression suite never needs updating","correct":false,"why":"Automated regression tests must be maintained as the product changes."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Automating regression tests allows the ever-growing suite to run quickly and frequently, for example on every build, so the team retains fast feedback within short iterations. The suite still needs maintenance and does not replace testing of new features.$L$, $L$The automated regression pack runs on each nightly build, so the team learns by morning whether any existing behaviour was broken, without spending days on manual re-checking.$L$
