select c.id, $L$mock1-01$L$, $L$Fundamentals of Testing$L$, 1, $L$K1$L$, 1, 1, $L$Which statement best describes what software testing is?$L$, $J$[{"text":"A set of activities to discover defects and evaluate the quality of software work products","correct":true,"why":"The syllabus defines testing as a set of activities to discover defects and evaluate the quality of software artifacts, not just running code."},{"text":"A process that runs only after the code is complete to prove the software has no defects","correct":false,"why":"Testing is not confined to post-coding execution and can never prove the absence of defects; both ideas are common misconceptions."},{"text":"The activity of correcting the defects found in the source code","correct":false,"why":"Correcting defects is debugging, a development activity, not testing."},{"text":"A purely administrative process of writing documents that describe the software","correct":false,"why":"Testing includes many non-documentation activities such as analysis, design, and execution, and its purpose is evaluation, not documentation."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$The ISTQB syllabus (Fundamentals of Testing) explains that testing is more than executing tests; it is a set of activities that both discover defects and evaluate the quality of work products. This includes static activities such as reviews as well as dynamic execution.$L$, $L$On an e-commerce checkout project, a tester reviews the requirements document for ambiguities and later executes payment scenarios, both of which count as testing.$L$
