select c.id, $L$mock1-06$L$, $L$Fundamentals of Testing$L$, 1, $L$K2$L$, 1, 6, $L$How do quality assurance and testing relate to each other?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Quality assurance is process-oriented and improves how work is done, while testing is product-oriented and evaluates the work products","correct":true,"why":"The syllabus contrasts QA (process focus, prevention through good process) with testing (product focus, detecting failures and evaluating quality)."},{"text":"Testing and quality assurance are identical terms with no difference","correct":false,"why":"They are related but distinct: QA targets the process, testing targets the product."},{"text":"Quality assurance replaces the need for testing when processes are mature","correct":false,"why":"Good processes reduce defects but do not remove the need to evaluate the product through testing."},{"text":"Testing focuses on the process while quality assurance focuses on the product","correct":false,"why":"This reverses the two: QA is process-oriented and testing is product-oriented."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$In Fundamentals of Testing, quality assurance focuses on adherence to proper processes to provide confidence that quality will be achieved, whereas testing is one form of quality control that evaluates actual work products. Both contribute to overall quality management.$L$, $L$A QA lead defines a mandatory code-review checklist for the whole team (process), while testers execute integration tests against the banking service to find failures (product).$L$
