select c.id, $L$mock1-12$L$, $L$Static Testing$L$, 3, $L$K1$L$, 1, 12, $L$Which of the following BEST describes static testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Examining work products such as requirements, code, and design without executing them","correct":true,"why":"Static testing evaluates work products manually or with tools but never runs the software under test."},{"text":"Running the software with test data and comparing actual to expected results","correct":false,"why":"That describes dynamic testing, where the code is executed."},{"text":"Measuring code coverage during test execution","correct":false,"why":"Coverage measurement requires executing the code, so it is a dynamic activity."},{"text":"Deploying the build to a production-like environment for a smoke test","correct":false,"why":"A smoke test executes the software, making it dynamic testing."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Static testing assesses work products through examination (reviews) or tool-based analysis without executing the code. Dynamic testing, by contrast, requires running the software.$L$, $L$Before any code is written, a business analyst has the team review the requirements document to catch ambiguities early.$L$
