select c.id, $L$mock2-12$L$, $L$Static Testing$L$, 3, $L$K1$L$, 2, 12, $L$Which of the following is a typical benefit of static testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Detecting and correcting defects earlier and improving communication among stakeholders","correct":true,"why":"Early defect detection and better shared understanding are recognized benefits of static testing."},{"text":"Measuring the actual response time of the system under load","correct":false,"why":"Response time under load is measured by dynamic performance testing."},{"text":"Confirming that the deployed system behaves correctly for end users","correct":false,"why":"Confirming runtime behavior requires executing the system."},{"text":"Producing code coverage metrics for the test suite","correct":false,"why":"Coverage metrics come from executing the code, a dynamic activity."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Static testing benefits include early defect detection, reduced development cost and time, improved product quality, and better communication and shared understanding among participants.$L$, $L$During a design review, developers and testers reach a shared understanding of an interface, avoiding integration surprises later.$L$
