select c.id, $L$mock2-13$L$, $L$Static Testing$L$, 3, $L$K2$L$, 2, 13, $L$A defect that is NOT easily found by dynamic testing but often surfaces in static testing is:$L$, $J$[{"text":"Unreachable or dead code and deviations from coding standards","correct":true,"why":"Dead code may never execute, so dynamic tests miss it, while a static review or analyzer flags it directly."},{"text":"A performance bottleneck under heavy concurrent load","correct":false,"why":"Concurrency and load issues generally require executing the system."},{"text":"A crash triggered by a specific runtime input value","correct":false,"why":"A runtime crash on specific input is found by executing the software."},{"text":"Incorrect calculation results at run time","correct":false,"why":"Wrong runtime results are typically exposed by dynamic testing."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Static testing can find defects that are hard or impossible to detect dynamically, such as unreachable code, coding standard violations, and inconsistencies, because they may never be exercised at run time.$L$, $L$A static analysis tool flags a block of code after a return statement that can never run, which no functional test would ever have reached.$L$
