select c.id, $L$mock2-32$L$, $L$Test Management$L$, 6, $L$K2$L$, 2, 32, $L$Which metric most directly reflects test case status during execution?$L$, $J$[{"text":"The number of test cases passed, failed, blocked and not yet run","correct":true,"why":"Pass, fail, blocked and not-run counts are exactly the test case status information used to track execution progress."},{"text":"The total lines of source code in the application","correct":false,"why":"Code size is a product characteristic, not a status of test execution."},{"text":"The hourly cost of the test environment","correct":false,"why":"Environment cost is a budget metric and does not describe how many tests have run."},{"text":"The number of stakeholders attending the test review","correct":false,"why":"Meeting attendance has no bearing on the execution status of test cases."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Test case status metrics report how many planned tests have been executed and with what result, typically passed, failed, blocked, or still to run. They are a primary indicator of execution progress.$L$, $L$The test lead posts a burndown: of 500 planned cases, 420 have run (390 passed, 30 failed) and 15 are blocked awaiting an environment fix, so 65 remain to be executed.$L$
