  (course_id, ext_key, syllabus_topic, module_number, k_level, mock, mock_order, question_text, options, explanation, workplace_example)
select c.id, $L$mock2-39$L$, $L$Test Tools$L$, 9, $L$K1$L$, 2, 39, $L$Which type of tool is used specifically to generate, populate, or mask realistic inputs so that tests have appropriate data to run against?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Test data preparation tools","correct":true,"why":"These tools create, select, generate or anonymise data so tests can execute against representative inputs."},{"text":"Defect management tools","correct":false,"why":"Defect tools track and manage reported defects, not the preparation of test data."},{"text":"Coverage tools","correct":false,"why":"Coverage tools measure what was exercised, not prepare data."},{"text":"Continuous integration tools","correct":false,"why":"CI tools orchestrate build and test pipelines, not specifically prepare or mask test data."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Test data preparation tools support building or provisioning the data a test needs - generating volumes of records, selecting subsets, or masking production data so it can be used safely. Good data is often the bottleneck, so these tools remove a common obstacle.$L$, $L$To test a loan-approval rule, a tester needs 5,000 customer records across many credit bands. A data preparation tool generates and masks them from production so no real personal data is exposed while still giving realistic coverage.$L$
