  (course_id, ext_key, syllabus_topic, module_number, k_level, mock, mock_order, question_text, options, explanation, workplace_example)
select c.id, $L$mock2-40$L$, $L$Agile Testing$L$, 10, $L$K2$L$, 2, 40, $L$Which is a genuine benefit of the whole-team approach for testing?$L$, $J$[{"text":"Testers, developers and business representatives collaborate closely, improving communication and shared understanding","correct":true,"why":"Close collaboration and direct communication reduce misunderstandings and let defects be prevented or found earlier."},{"text":"It removes the need for any testing activities","correct":false,"why":"Collaboration does not replace testing; it strengthens it."},{"text":"It means developers never need to talk to testers","correct":false,"why":"The whole-team approach increases, not removes, developer-tester interaction."},{"text":"It guarantees a completely defect-free product","correct":false,"why":"No approach can guarantee zero defects; that is an unrealistic expectation."}]$J$::jsonb, $L$Benefits of the whole-team approach include enhanced communication and collaboration, drawing on the full range of skills for the benefit of the project, and making testing and development complementary activities. It does not eliminate testing or guarantee perfection.$L$, $L$A tester joins the developers at a three-amigos discussion so ambiguous acceptance criteria are clarified before coding starts, preventing a defect rather than finding it later.$L$
